            <div type="translation" xml:lang="en" resp="#AA">
                <p>
                    Sextus Hortensius, son of Aulus, of tribe Stellatina [and] Sextus Hortensius Clarus, master of the Lares, assistant to Germanicus Caesar when consul, superintended the building of a forum and Augusteum, on private land, with their 
                    own money, together with 57 statues around the porticoes, pools, and sewers; the same men also dedicated it and gave cakes and a banquet.
                </p>
